    "goal": "Reproduce mid-range arterial wall shear stress (15 dyn/cm² = 1.5 Pa) on a HUVEC-lined arterial microchannel.",
    "rationale": "Target wall shear 1.5 Pa (15 dyn/cm²) is mid-range arterial shear. Chose a standard arterial OOC channel geometry of 1000 µm wide × 200 µm tall × 20 mm long. Using flow_rate_for_shear_stress, 600 µL/min achieves exactly 1.5 Pa at medium viscosity 1e-3 Pa·s. Verified: wall_shear_stress returns 1.5 Pa; Reynolds ≈ 16.7 (well-laminar, ≪2300); pressure drop over 20 mm ≈ 300 Pa (well within syringe-pump capability); residence time ≈ 0.4 s. HUVEC seeded at 15,000 cells/cm² (mid-range of the 1e4–2e4 registry range) over the 2 cm² channel area = 30,000 cells/channel. Note: HUVEC registry shear range is microvascular (0.1–1 Pa); 1.5 Pa is above that and represents arterial shear, which is the explicit goal here — endothelial morphology/junction markers are the readout, not TEER.",
